; T-0015D golden: belgeodesy.zmp - static array [1..50] (low bound 1), two top-level 'var'
; sections, 'while' string padding, index out of the INITIALISED range at P4.
; dx/dy filled only for indices 1..9; xx:=IntToStr(GetX-dx[GetZ-6]), yy similarly, each
; left-zero-padded to 4 via a 'while length(s)<4 do s:="0"+s' loop.
; ResultURL := GetURLBase+IntToStr(GetZ-6)+'/'+xx+yy+'.png'
; P3 (GetZ-6=8, in the filled range): dx[8]=4637, dy[8]=2553 -> xx=IntToStr(1234-4637)=
;   '-3403' (len 5, no padding applied since the while condition length<4 is already false),
;   yy=IntToStr(5678-2553)='3125' (len 4, no padding needed).
; P4 (GetZ-6=12, WITHIN the array's [1..50] declared bounds but past the filled 1..9, so
;   I1 zero-init applies, not an out-of-range fault): dx[12]=dy[12]=0 -> xx='131071',
;   yy='87654' (both already len>=4, unpadded) -> the golden records legacy's behaviour, not
;   a 'sensible' one.
; P1 (GetZ-6=-5) and P2 (GetZ-6=-4) index BELOW the array's declared low bound 1. This is NOT
; undefined (docs/handoffs/T-0015D-review.md finding 2, correcting the earlier "no compiler
; stack layout" reasoning below): the scripts run in the PascalScript VM, not compiled Delphi
; code, and the VM range-checks every static-array index at run time
; (uPSRuntime.pas:7127-7135/:7289-7297, `if Param >= Size then CMD_Err2(erCustomError,
; 'Static array index out of bounds (%d). Length is %d.')`).
; T-0032 CORRECTION (superseding the two ErrorText values T-0015D wrote): `Param` here is NOT
; the script's raw index. For a non-constant index expression (`dx[GetZ-6]` - GetZ is a runtime
; bound variable, not a compile-time literal), the COMPILER itself subtracts the array's declared
; low bound BEFORE the generic array-access opcode ever runs: `TPSPascalCompiler`'s array-index
; codegen (uPSCompiler.pas ~6965-6988) builds `TPSBinValueOp(otSub){Val1:=<index expr>,
; Val2:=StartOffset}` and stores the S32 result into a `btU32` (Cardinal) temp register
; (`AllocStackReg(FindBaseType(btU32))`); `TPSExec.ReadVariable`'s `VarType=3` case
; (uPSRuntime.pas:7158-7233) then reads `Param` FROM that Cardinal temp (`Param :=
; PPSVariantU32(Tmp).Data`), not from the raw index. So for `dx: array[1..50]` (StartOffset=1):
; P1: index=GetZ-6=1-6=-5, Param=Cardinal(-5-1)=Cardinal(-6)=4294967290.
; P2: index=GetZ-6=2-6=-4, Param=Cardinal(-4-1)=Cardinal(-5)=4294967291.
; (Contrast the CONSTANT-index case used by the fill loop above, `dx[1]:=36` etc.: there the
; compiler folds `index-StartOffset` itself, at COMPILE time, via `TPSSubNumber.SubNo :=
; Cardinal(GetInt(...)-StartOffset)` - same subtraction, just done earlier - so `dx[1]` addresses
; element 0, consistent with the fold below and with megafonpro's StartOffset=0 arrays, where the
; subtraction is a no-op and this correction does not apply.)
; So both P1 and P2 end in a defined script runtime error -
; "Static array index out of bounds (4294967290). Length is 50." at P1,
; "Static array index out of bounds (4294967291). Length is 50." at P2 - and `buildRequest`
; fails before `xx`/`yy` are ever computed. Added below as expected-error sections.
;
; PD-1 (port defect, renamed from PD-101 - see docs/handoffs/T-0015D.md, finding 3): the
; interpreter (src/sas/script/interpreter.cpp evalIndex/IndexAssign) supported element indexing
; ('s[i]') only on ValueKind::Str/Empty; ValueKind::Array (any 'arr[i]' or 'arr[i]:=v', including
; this script's very first statement dx[1]:=36) returned ErrorCode::Unsupported, so every section
; of this map failed end-to-end through UrlScript::buildRequest - P3/P4's value goldens and
; P1/P2's expected-error goldens alike, before either the arithmetic or the range check above ever
; ran. FIXED by T-0032 - see docs/handoffs/T-0032.md.

